hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19262","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Jad narrated to us from al-Hasan ibn Abdullah that Amr ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to him that he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat a shoulder, then stand, rinse his mouth, pray, and not perform wudu."
